{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27105942","formula":"C₂₀H₁₄O₈","hill":"C20H14O8","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":14.0,"O":8.0},"names":{"en":"Bikaverin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bikaverin is a red polyketide pigment made by several fungi, most of them species of Fusarium. It is a tetracyclic benzoxanthone and was first characterised in 1971 from Gibberella fujikuroi, the fungus better known as the industrial source of gibberellins. Bikaverin kills some protozoa and oomycetes, is toxic to a range of tumour cell lines, and has been studied as a natural colourant."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":5281730,"mass":382.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=CC2=C1C(=O)C3=C(C4=C(C(=C3O2)O)C(=O)C(=CC4=O)OC)O)OC","inchikey":"ZOQMSOSJEWBMHP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"6,11-dihydroxy-3,8-dimethoxy-1-methylbenzo[b]xanthene-7,10,12-trione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5281730","atoms":42,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.368,"y":-1.297,"z":-0.047,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.005,"y":2.916,"z":0.003,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.933,"y":-2.61,"z":-0.132,"el":"O"},{"x":1.543,"y":2.789,"z":0.059,"el":"O"},{"x":6.095,"y":-1.647,"z":0.047,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.904,"y":-1.27,"z":-0.213,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.505,"y":-2.534,"z":-0.191,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.555,"y":2.808,"z":-0.058,"el":"O"},{"x":0.207,"y":0.851,"z":-0.02,"el":"C"},{"x":0.22,"y":-0.542,"z":-0.054,"el":"C"},{"x":2.708,"y":0.743,"z":0.033,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.209,"y":0.844,"z":-0.076,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.202,"y":-0.552,"z":-0.11,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.002,"y":1.552,"z":-0.03,"el":"C"},{"x":1.491,"y":1.569,"z":0.027,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.986,"y":-1.246,"z":-0.099,"el":"C"},{"x":2.575,"y":-0.645,"z":-0.004,"el":"C"},{"x":3.973,"y":1.334,"z":0.075,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.469,"y":-1.309,"z":-0.158,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.485,"y":1.585,"z":-0.087,"el":"C"},{"x":3.717,"y":-1.